WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
Compliance basics, described accurately.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.464
This is orientation, not legal advice.

3
00:00:05.744 --> 00:00:11.035
The point is to know which questions to bring to your privacy or legal colleagues, early.

4
00:00:11.315 --> 00:00:29.043
GDPR (the EU’s General Data Protection Regulation) applies to personal data of people in the EU, and its Article 5 principles map directly onto logging decisions: purpose limitation (collect for specified purposes and don’t repurpose incompatibly;

5
00:00:29.323 --> 00:00:42.933
“debugging” and “training an internal model on customer chats” are different purposes), data minimisation (only what’s necessary), and storage limitation (keep identifiable data no longer than necessary).

6
00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:46.072
Pseudonymized logs are still in scope, as above.

7
00:00:46.352 --> 00:00:49.787
Other jurisdictions have their own laws with different details.

8
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.541
Health data in the US brings in HIPAA.

9
00:00:52.821 --> 00:01:05.408
You can see the shape of the requirement in how providers package it: Anthropic offers HIPAA-ready API access only with a signed business associate agreement (BAA) and only for eligible features.

10
00:01:05.688 --> 00:01:15.245
Any other vendor that could receive protected health information through your system, your observability vendor included, needs the same review with your compliance team.

11
00:01:15.525 --> 00:01:28.155
Contracts and customer commitments often matter more day to day than statutes: enterprise customers commonly specify where data may be processed, how long it may be kept, and which subprocessors may see it.

12
00:01:28.435 --> 00:01:30.739
Your tracing vendor is a subprocessor.

13
00:01:31.019 --> 00:01:33.835
The engineer’s job is not to interpret the law.

14
00:01:34.115 --> 00:01:45.741
It’s to make the data flows legible (which copies exist, where, for how long, who can read them), to default to collecting less, and to raise the question before launch rather than after an incident.

15
00:01:46.021 --> 00:01:55.365
A one-page data-flow diagram of your LLM system, with every store and its retention, is the most useful thing you can bring to that conversation.
